 :context
 "Ongoing careful, smaller-batch rollout (capable model + mandatory verification per
  agent) after a prior 18-agent haiku batch had a 61% defect rate. 48+ consecutive
  agents on this stricter protocol succeeded before this one. Built from
  cloud-itonami-isic-0123 (growing of citrus fruits) as the module-structure
  template, with clojure -M:test independently re-run from fresh clones before and
  after push. Registry entry independently re-verified fresh before any work began:
  {:id \"0124\" :name \"Growing of pome fruits and stone fruits\" ...} genuinely
  matches (no ID/name mismatch, a known failure mode in this fleet). No prior
  repository existed at cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-0124 or the stale
  gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-A0124 placeholder (404 confirmed)."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["direct field-equipment operation (grower's exclusive authority)"
  "finalizing a spray-application decision (agronomist/grower authority)"
  "harvest-timing / replanting economic decisions (remain human authority)"]

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-0124 with Governor, Facts, Registry, Store, Advisor,
  Phase, Operation, Sim (mirrors cloud-itonami-isic-0123 module-for-module,
  namespace pomestoneops.*):
  - Governor (PomeStoneOperationsGovernor): 5 hard checks (orchard-not-registered,
    no-execution, field-equipment-or-spray-blocked, op-not-allowed,
    orchard-count-invalid) + 3 escalation gates (always-escalate crop-health
    concern, cost-threshold supply orders, low confidence < 0.7)
  - Facts: supply categories with cost thresholds (seedling/fertilizer/equipment),
    fruit classes (apple/pear/quince = pome; peach/plum/cherry/apricot = stone)
  - Registry: independent pure predicates (cost-exceeds-threshold?,
    orchard-count-non-positive?, confidence-below-floor?)
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore (registered-orchard lookup)
  - Advisor: Advisor protocol + MockAdvisor (4 ops)
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout gate
  - Operation: composes advisor -> governor -> phase-gate (langgraph-clj wiring
    deferred, matching 0123's own stub)
  - Sim: demo runner with a working -main
  - Operations: log-orchard-record, schedule-field-operation,
    flag-crop-health-concern (e.g. codling moth/fire blight, always escalates),
    order-supplies (closed allowlist, :effect :propose)
  - Tests: 31 tests / 105 assertions (facts, governor, phase, registry, store), all
    green -- one extra deftest vs 0123's 30 (fire-blight-specific escalation case)
    plus wider fact coverage (7 fruit classes with a pome/stone :group dimension)
  - All .cljc (portable, no JVM interop), AGPL-3.0-or-later
  - README/business-model/operator-guide describe the real API"

 :consequences
 {:positive
  ["Pome/stone-fruit-growing (0124) now genuinely implemented and fully tested"
   "Scope boundaries (field-equipment operation, spray-application finalization)
